{"name":"Mini Cake","hex":"#fbf6de","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mini","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Miniature, tiny, small."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Abbreviation of miniskirt.","Abbreviation of minicomputer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mini"},{"term":"cake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich, sweet dessert food, typically made of flour, sugar, and eggs and baked in an oven, and often covered in icing.","A small mass of baked dough, especially a thin loaf from unleavened dough."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Coat (something) with a crust of solid material.","To form into a cake, or mass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mini","blocks":[{"text":"The Mini is a two-door, four-seat small car produced for four decades over a single generation, with many names and variants, by the British Motor Corporation (BMC) and its successors British Leyland and the Rover Group, and finally (briefly) under BMW ownership. Minis were built as saloons, estates, convertibles, and various other body styles. Minus a brief 1990s hiatus, from 1959 into 2000, an estimated 5.38 million of all variations combined were built."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Morris_Mini-Minor_1959_%28621_AOK%29.jpg/330px-Morris_Mini-Minor_1959_%28621_AOK%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mini","wikidata":"Q36024"},{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining flour with a liquid, a fat or both, and usually with a leavening agent. Cakes are usually baked, but can be griddled. In their oldest forms, cakes were modifications of bread, but cakes now cover a wide range of preparations that can be simple or elaborate and which share features with other desserts such as pastries, meringues, custards, and pies."}],"image":